#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""SlumsMS monitor (tickets 42 and 46): health checks with Discord alerts, a status message and release news.

    slumsms-monitor check  <target> [--dry-run] [--verbose]   run every check once, alert / recover (timer: 1 min)
    slumsms-monitor status <target> [--dry-run]               post or edit the server status message (timer: 5 min)
    slumsms-monitor news   <target> [--file F] [--seed] [--dry-run]
                                                              post launcher news entries not posted yet
    slumsms-monitor test-webhook <target> [alerts|status|news] send one test message

A target is a server to watch. Its settings are in /etc/slumsms-monitor/<target>.conf (KEY=VALUE, not secret) and its
webhook URLs in /etc/slumsms-monitor/<target>.env (root-only, 0600, never in git). Without a webhook URL every message
goes to the local log only (/var/log/slumsms-monitor/<target>.log). State lives in /var/lib/slumsms-monitor/<target>/.

Python 3 standard library plus PyYAML (for the server's config.yaml). Read-only towards the server: it runs systemctl
show/is-active, journalctl, jstat, docker inspect/exec (SELECT only) and HTTP GETs; it never starts or stops anything.
"""
